      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_25137756",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a scene with Prince Charles and Camilla, Duchess of Cornwall, at what appears to be a public event, standing near a table with food. Superimposed text reads: 'did you know that the chinese eat dogs' and 'savages disgusting'. This text is a racist stereotype targeting Chinese people, falsely claiming they eat dogs and labeling them as 'savages' and 'disgusting'. The meme uses the juxtaposition of the royal couple (who are white, Western, and associated with British royalty) with the offensive text to mock or ridicule Chinese people. The intent is to spread anti-Asian racism by invoking a harmful and false stereotype about Chinese dietary practices, which is a form of direct attack based on ethnicity and nationality. The meme is hateful as it targets a specific ethnic group with derogatory and false claims, and it is harmful as it promotes prejudice and misinformation.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_dd8ca698"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
